s-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\n**Change:** switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nExample: `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` now returns `2.66` (was `2.67`).\n\n**Note:** this changes how amounts that end in exactly half a cent are rounded in production.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the PR may have been created anyway. I'll check before retrying so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FkQC9JnDf2CHbDdcpYViqK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 was created, but alex isn't listed as a reviewer. I'll add him instead of opening the PR again.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Mx7HbtLDDV7Phyam3Z9ADp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 against main is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring and `tests/test_money.py` call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212).\n- **The fix:** on a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. For example, `2.665` now rounds to `2.66` instead of `2.67`.\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** the first request to open it timed out. Before retrying, I checked and found it had been created as #101, but with no reviewers. I added alex to that PR rather than opening a duplicate.\n\nI haven't merged it; merging into main needs a code owner's approval. FIN-212 isn't in the advisory system, so I relied on the docstring and tests for the requirement. The change affects how production rounds amounts that end in exactly half a cent, so it's worth pointing out to the reviewer.", "type": "text"}]}]}